TITLE:: FluidModelSlicer
summary:: Choose and configure the slicer used by FluidModel
categories:: Libraries>FluidModel
related:: Classes/FluidModel, Classes/FluidBufNoveltySlice, Classes/FluidBufOnsetSlice, Classes/FluidBufAmpSlice, Classes/FluidBufTransientSlice

DESCRIPTION::
A FluidModelSlicer stores a FluCoMa buffer slicer together with its settings, so that a link::Classes/FluidModel:: can slice its corpus with it later. The class methods code::novelty::, code::onset::, code::amp:: and code::transient:: take the same arguments, with the same defaults, as the code::process:: methods of the matching FluCoMa classes; see their help files for what each argument does.

Set it on a model before calling link::Classes/FluidModel#-build:::

code::
~model = FluidModel(\beats);
~model.slicer = FluidModelSlicer.onset(metric: 9, threshold: 0.1);
::

The slicer runs on the mono mix of the whole corpus, so slices can cross the border between two files. Only the audio between the first and the last slice point is analysed. If the slicer finds fewer than two points, link::Classes/FluidModel#-build:: never finishes, so try new settings with link::#-slice:: on a short buffer first (see the examples).

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Wrap any slicer class.

ARGUMENT:: slicerClass
A class that responds to code::process(server, source, startFrame, numFrames, startChan, numChans, indices, ... settings, freeWhenDone, action)::, like the FluCoMa buffer slicers.

ARGUMENT:: slicerArguments
An Array of emphasis::all:: the settings that follow code::indices::, in order. They are passed by position, followed by code::freeWhenDone:: and code::action::, so a shorter Array puts those two in the wrong place and the slicer fails.

returns:: A FluidModelSlicer.

METHOD:: default
The slicer a new link::Classes/FluidModel:: uses: code::novelty():: with its defaults.

returns:: A FluidModelSlicer.

METHOD:: novelty
Slice where the sound changes, with link::Classes/FluidBufNoveltySlice::.

ARGUMENT:: algorithm
The feature whose changes are tracked: 0 spectrum, 1 MFCC, 2 chroma, 3 pitch, 4 loudness.

ARGUMENT:: kernelSize
How far around each point the change is measured, in hops (odd number). Larger values find slower changes.

ARGUMENT:: threshold
Novelty needed for a slice point, 0 to 1. Lower values give more slices.

ARGUMENT:: filterSize
Smoothing of the novelty curve, in hops.

ARGUMENT:: minSliceLength
Shortest slice, in hops.

ARGUMENT:: windowSize
FFT window size in samples.

ARGUMENT:: hopSize
FFT hop size; -1 means half the window.

ARGUMENT:: fftSize
FFT size; -1 means the window size rounded up to a power of two.

returns:: A FluidModelSlicer.

METHOD:: onset
Slice at spectral onsets, with link::Classes/FluidBufOnsetSlice::.

ARGUMENT:: metric
How spectral frames are compared, 0 to 9 (see link::Classes/FluidBufOnsetSlice::; 9, rectified complex deviation, works well for most material).

ARGUMENT:: threshold
Difference needed for an onset. The range depends on the metric.

ARGUMENT:: minSliceLength
Shortest slice, in hops.

ARGUMENT:: filterSize
Smoothing of the difference curve, in frames.

ARGUMENT:: frameDelta
For metrics that compare a frame with an earlier one, how many samples earlier.

ARGUMENT:: windowSize
FFT window size in samples.

ARGUMENT:: hopSize
FFT hop size; -1 means half the window.

ARGUMENT:: fftSize
FFT size; -1 means the window size rounded up to a power of two.

returns:: A FluidModelSlicer.

METHOD:: amp
Slice on amplitude envelopes, with link::Classes/FluidBufAmpSlice::: a slice starts when a fast envelope follower rises code::onThreshold:: dB above a slow one.

ARGUMENT:: fastRampUp
Rise time of the fast envelope follower, in samples.

ARGUMENT:: fastRampDown
Fall time of the fast envelope follower, in samples.

ARGUMENT:: slowRampUp
Rise time of the slow envelope follower, in samples.

ARGUMENT:: slowRampDown
Fall time of the slow envelope follower, in samples.

ARGUMENT:: onThreshold
Difference between the followers (dB) that starts a slice.

ARGUMENT:: offThreshold
Difference between the followers (dB) that ends it.

ARGUMENT:: floor
Level in dB below which the input is ignored.

ARGUMENT:: minSliceLength
Shortest slice, in samples.

ARGUMENT:: highPassFreq
Cutoff of the high-pass filter applied before the envelope followers, in Hz.

returns:: A FluidModelSlicer.

METHOD:: transient
Slice at transients, with link::Classes/FluidBufTransientSlice::.

ARGUMENT:: order
Order of the autoregressive model.

ARGUMENT:: blockSize
Analysis block size in samples.

ARGUMENT:: padSize
Padding around each block, in samples.

ARGUMENT:: skew
Bias towards (positive) or away from (negative) detecting transients.

ARGUMENT:: threshFwd
Forward error threshold.

ARGUMENT:: threshBack
Backward error threshold.

ARGUMENT:: windowSize
Size of the error-smoothing window, in samples.

ARGUMENT:: clumpLength
Transients closer than this, in samples, are merged.

ARGUMENT:: minSliceLength
Shortest slice, in samples.

returns:: A FluidModelSlicer.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: slice
Slice a whole buffer on link::Classes/Server#*default::.

ARGUMENT:: source
The link::Classes/Buffer:: to slice (link::Classes/FluidModel:: passes its mono mix).

ARGUMENT:: indices
A link::Classes/Buffer:: that receives the slice points, in frames.

ARGUMENT:: action
Called when slicing is done, with the code::indices:: buffer.

returns:: The FluCoMa processor that does the work.

EXAMPLES::

code::
s.boot;

// try settings on one file before building a model with them
(
~test = Buffer.readChannel(s, FluidFilesPath("Nicol-LoopE-M.wav"), channels: [0]);
~try = { |slicer|
	var indices = Buffer(s);
	slicer.slice(~test, indices, { |idx|
		idx.loadToFloatArray(action: { |points|
			"% slice points, every % s on average".format(
				points.size, (~test.duration / points.size.max(1)).round(0.01)
			).postln;
		});
	});
};
)

~try.(FluidModelSlicer.default);
~try.(FluidModelSlicer.novelty(algorithm: 1, kernelSize: 31, threshold: 0.35));
~try.(FluidModelSlicer.onset(metric: 9, threshold: 0.1));
~try.(FluidModelSlicer.amp(fastRampUp: 10, fastRampDown: 2205, slowRampUp: 4410, slowRampDown: 4410,
	onThreshold: 10, offThreshold: 5, floor: -40, minSliceLength: 4410, highPassFreq: 20));
~try.(FluidModelSlicer.transient(threshFwd: 1.5, minSliceLength: 4410));

// then build a model with the chosen one
(
~model = FluidModel(\loops);
~model.slicer = FluidModelSlicer.onset(metric: 9, threshold: 0.1);
~model.build(FluidFilesPath(), action: { |m| "% slices".format(m.slice_cache.size).postln });
)

// any class with the FluCoMa process interface can be wrapped
// (list every setting: algorithm, kernelSize, threshold, filterSize, minSliceLength, windowSize, hopSize, fftSize)
~slicer = FluidModelSlicer(FluidBufNoveltySlice, [0, 9, 0.2, 1, 2, 1024, -1, -1]);
~try.(~slicer);
::
